# ============================================================
# Claude Code skills — never ignore anything inside a skill
# (skills bundle their own node_modules, lib/, etc. — partial
# tracking breaks them at runtime)
# ============================================================
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**

# ============================================================
# DEV BUILDS — never committed, because this repo is PUBLIC and
# games/<slug>/output/ is what the GitHub Pages portal serves.
# A --dev build arms dev_mode_enabled at StoryInit, which renders the
# <<devJumps>> sidebar (skip to any chapter) plus the stat-adjustment
# controls. Publishing one hands every player the whole game at once.
# So dev builds go to games/<slug>/output_dev/ and stay local — which
# is still reachable from a phone, since Live Server is rooted at
# story_gen/ and Tailscale reaches that. ship-gate: no --dev, no --debug.
# ============================================================
games/*/output_dev/

# ============================================================
# twine-game-explorer: browser profiles, saves, screenshots
# (binary/transient runtime output — not source)
# ============================================================
game_explorations/*/manual/profile/
game_explorations/*/profile/
game_explorations/*/screenshots/live/
game_explorations/*/archive/
game_explorations/*/.live/

# ============================================================
# Playable output media is TRACKED for LIVE-on-the-portal games (the
# portal needs it). Overrides the blanket videos/ + media-extension
# ignores above. Re-include the dir first, then its contents — git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is still excluded.
# Add a game's output/videos here when it goes live on the portal.
# ============================================================
!games/vesper/output/videos/
!games/vesper/output/videos/**

# Media Lab is the ORIGINAL query-study rig and the arm-A baseline every later run
# is compared against — and since 2026-07-31 it also carries the first live
# `pool_dir` slot (lab_behind_t5, four clips the engine cycles). Its media was
# never whitelisted, so every one of its refs 404'd on the portal while _c and _d
# rendered fine. 13 files, 24 MB. The source games/media_lab/videos/ stays ignored —
# only the output copy the portal actually serves is tracked.
!games/media_lab/output/videos/
!games/media_lab/output/videos/**


# ============================================================
# find-media working evidence (harvest dumps, montages, candidate
# jsonl, raw transcripts) — large + transient, never source.
# ============================================================
**/.find-media/

# ============================================================
# Heavy experiments / scratch — local only, not part of the engine.
# ============================================================
test_blender/
avatar_prototype/
games/media_testbed/
# The WHOLE research corpus is local-only now (2026-07-09). It was 806 MB of the ~1.0 GB tracked tree,
# which pushed the published GitHub Pages site over its 1 GB hard limit -> every build after b067942
# failed with "Page build failed". Untracked with `git rm -r --cached` (files kept on disk, and the
# history still has them), so the portal publishes ~263 MB and builds again. Supersedes the two
# sub-dir entries below.
game_explorations/
game_explorations/vesper_coverplay/
game_explorations/vesper_wardrobe/

# playwright-skill temp execution files (transient)
**/.temp-execution-*.js

# python bytecode inside the skills tree (the !.claude/skills/** negation above un-ignores it)
.claude/skills/**/__pycache__/

# ============================================================
# Patreon posting folder — on disk, deliberately NOT tracked.
# This repo is PUBLIC (storygen-beep/Story-Gen) and serves GitHub Pages, so
# tier/pricing strategy, cadence analysis and the compliance notes must not be
# pushed. Same treatment as game_explorations/ above: kept locally, out of git.
# ============================================================
patreon/

# ============================================================
# Resume / job-application material — on disk, deliberately NOT tracked.
# This repo is PUBLIC (verified 2026-09-02 via `gh repo view`: visibility PUBLIC),
# so personal data must never reach it: once pushed it is in the history and in
# anyone's clone, and deleting the file later does not remove it. Same treatment
# as patreon/ and game_explorations/ above.
# ============================================================
/resume/
